!Proposed definitions



{BOX()}

!!cmavo: fi'o (FIhO)



!!!Proposed Definition

Converts a selbri into a tag. The tag modifies a sentence or connects two sentences. When modifying a sentence, the tag can take an argument that further specifies it and which fills the first argument of the converted selbri. 

!!!See Also

* {fe'u}



!!!Proposed Keywords



!!!Usage Examples

;doi .deivid. do no roi klama lo cinri fi'o kansa mi:''David, you never come to interesting places with me.''

;lo citno nanla cu gleki catlu lo kacma fi'o se jbini lo pendo be ny:''The young boy looked happily into the camera, standing among his friends.''

;do facki fi la lojban. fi'o tadji fe'u ma:''You discovered Lojban by what method?''

{BOX}



{BOX()}

!!cmavo: fe'u (FEhU)



!!!Proposed Definition

Terminator for FIhO. 



!!!See Also

*{fi'o}



!!!Proposed Keywords



!!!Usage Examples

;lo fi'o kansa fe'u klama cu gleki:''The accompanied goer is happy.''

{BOX}





!!Formal definitions



||broda fi'o brode ko'a| |broda .i joi ko'a brode||



The connection between the two relationships is {joi}, not {je}, because the two relationships are not independent of each other. They are inextricably linked, but what exactly the link is is not specified and 

can vary with context.



